00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:35.000
Peter didn't require a special formula at all. Police concocted the recipe, hoping it would compel the kidnapper to visit a pharmacy. If the pharmacist recognized the very specific formula request, they could tip off detectives. The following day, a heavy-set man walked into a pharmacy in Stanford, Connecticut, about 40 miles away from Westbury. The man inquired about two of the ingredients listed in Peter's phony baby formula, vitamin B12 and dozex. The pharmacist didn't have the items available, so the man quickly left.

