00:22:35.000 --> 00:23:13.000
When police were informed, the unknown man was long gone and never identified. In the meantime, police started a thorough search for Peter in Westbury, despite believing with utmost certainty that their son was still alive. Betty and Morris felt increasingly anxious, as more than 100 police officers canvassed the streets around their home, peered down drains, lifted manhole covers, ripped apart bushes, and sifted through poles of soft dirt. It wouldn't have quelled Betty and Morris' anxiety when the media spun the police search as proof law enforcement assumed Peter was dead.

