00:25:31.000 --> 00:26:05.000
The police have given their word they won't interfere. Tomorrow is Sunday and the churches all over the city will be open. New York churches and synagogues supported the Weinbergers by keeping their doors open all day and all night. However, the kidnapper didn't show up. Days later, a telephone operator in New York received a call. The mail caller said, The kidnapped baby will be left in the 168th Street subway station. He then hung up.

